# Excave agent rules

## Before non-trivial work

1. Read `docs/STATE.md` first.
2. Read only docs needed for the task (`ARCHITECTURE`, `LOTS`, art docs).
3. Inspect the real code involved — do not trust stale docs.

## Source of truth

- **Code wins** over any document.
- If code ≠ `docs/STATE.md`: follow code; fix `STATE.md` in the same change when the global state shifted.

## Token budget

- Do **not** load all docs by default.
- Prefer `STATE.md` → then one specialized doc → then code.
- Do not paste long docs into replies; link paths.

## End of a lot

- Update `docs/STATE.md` if global state changed.
- Update `docs/LOTS.md`.
- Update a specialized doc only if necessary.
- Never put hypothetical future in `STATE.md` → use `docs/FUTURE_IDEAS.md`.
- Do not duplicate the same facts across many docs; link instead.

## Stable bricks (do not rewrite without a proven bug)

- Server authority
- Input-only movement (no client absolute position)
- Client prediction + ack replay
- Chunk AOI streaming
- Excavation secrets server-only

## Structuring constants

Before changing `TILE_SIZE`, `CHUNK_SIZE`, tick rates, collision footprint, AOI, etc.: search all usages in the repo.

## Finish checklist

- Run `pnpm test` / `typecheck` / `build` according to impact.
- Short compte rendu; **STOP** and wait for explicit `continue` before the next lot.
